Evaluate the candidate using checklist progress, domain analysis, and world-state prediction together.

Output format:
NEXT_STATE:
  Summary: <1-3 sentence high-level summary>
  File_Changes: <files modified/created and how, or none>
  Command_Output_Summary: <concise summary of expected stdout/stderr, or none>
  Progress: <Yes/No + short reason>
CHECKLIST_ITEM_SCORES:
{% for item in checklist_items %}
- Item {{ loop.index }}: <scalar 0.0-1.0>
- REASONING: <1-2 sentences>
{% endfor %}
DOMAIN_ANALYSIS:
  Specification: <brief note or none>
  Reasoning: <brief note or none>
  Coordination: <brief note or none>
REASONING: <2-5 sentences integrating checklist, domain, and world-model views>
{% if enable_verbal_feedback and verbal_feedback_mode == "feedback" %}
FEEDBACK: <one-line critique for the coding model's next step>
{% endif %}
REWARD: <scalar value between 0.0 and 1.0>

[[[CHECKLIST_SYSTEM_TEMPLATE]]]
You generate an issue-progress rubric (checklist) for a coding agent verifier.
Return YAML only. No prose outside YAML. Do not call tools.

Rubric requirements:
- 6 to 10 items.
- Each item must include: id, phase, weight, description, done_when.
- Ground items in concrete paths, symbols, or error strings from the issue/history.
- Include at least 2 integrity/safety items.

Output YAML format:
rubric:
  - id: D1
    phase: diagnose|reproduce|localize|fix|validate|cleanup
    weight: 1|2|3
    description: "<verb-first, concrete criterion>"
    done_when: "<observable condition>"

